From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mhavant <matthew.hoelting@avant.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:52:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(claude-native): read a teammate's message as the start of
 a lead turn

Claude starts a lead turn for a teammate's message without firing
UserPromptSubmit, and the OSC report and status file may not change, so
after a Stop that left teammates running, that turn read idle for its
whole length and follow-ups went straight into the busy pane.

The transcript reader now reports when a teammate message reached the
main thread, and the forwarder records that time as the session's latest
prompt, which the status pollers already treat as a turn start.

Not upstream yet: proposed alongside upstream PR #10849.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mhavant <matthew.hoelting@avant.com>
Docs: none (fix: a teammate-started lead turn reads as working; no setting)
